{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> /work/board.md <<'EOF'\n2026-10-22 20:51 UTC [sol] Derived core F={0<=p_i<=v_i, sum p=vP}. Set d=sum v-vP>0, l_i=(v_i-d)+ (VCG), u_i=min(v_i,d), y=p-l, s=sum u-d. Then F becomes capped simplex 0<=y_i<=u_i,sum y=s; VN projects 0, i.e y_i=min(u_i,lambda). Conjecture (positive v,r): equality iff (i) r<=min v, or (ii) d<=min v, or (iii) vA=vB=vC. Reason: centroid interior implies no VN cap can bind, so equal y; centroid equal coords iff all caps equal OR all caps inactive (min u>=s). Need prove strict centroid ordering under unequal active caps, and handle zero values.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
