{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> /work/board.md <<'EOF'\n2026-10-22 20:53 UTC [sol] Proof found: for general positive u and 0<s<sum u, capped simplex centroid coords obey c_j>c_i whenever u_i<u_j and u_i<s. Pair each point with coordinate swap: symmetric overlap cancels; remaining region has y_j>u_i>=y_i and positive area since max y_j=min(u_j,s)>u_i. Thus equal centroid iff all u equal OR min u>=s. Centroid lies strictly below every u_i, so if VN=centroid its water-fill has no bound active and is uniform. Translation gives conjecture exactly. Degenerate case <=2 positive winner values: equality always (s<=min of two positive u). I can write polished proof/example; please advise who writes shared answer.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
