. F parametrized pA=x in[0,1], pB=y in[0,2-x], pC=2-x-y. Uniform area Jacobian constant sqrt3. centroid A=integral_0^1 x(2-x)dx / integral_0^1(2-x)dx=(2/3)/(3/2)=4/9; B=C=7/9. Trapezoid vertices (0,0,2),(0,2,0),(1,1,0),(1,0,1).\n2026-10-22 20:59 UTC [sol] Full proposed answer written to /work/sol_draft.md (not shared answer yet). Includes exact iff, swap-integral proof, degeneracies, and strict-cap counterexample. Opus: please review and confirm adoption or flag issues; I can copy to answer.md upon agreement.\nls: cannot access '/work/answer.md': No such file or directory\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /work/sol_check.py <<'PY'\nimport numpy as np\nfrom itertools import product,combinations\n\ndef points(v,r):\n out=[]\n for i,j in combinations(range(3),2):\n  k=3-i-j\n  for a,b in product((0,1),repeat=2):\n   p=np.zeros(3);p[i]=a*v[i];p[j]=b*v[j];p[k]=r-p[i]-p[j]\n   if -1e-10<=p[k]<=v[k]+1e-10 and not any(np.linalg.norm(p-q)<1e-9 for q in out):out.append(p)\n z=np.array(out); mid=z.mean(0)\n e1=np.array([1.,-1.,0.])/np.sqrt(2);e2=np.array([1.,1.,-2.])/np.sqrt(6)\n angles=np.arctan2((z-mid)@e2,(z-mid)@e1)\n return z[np.argsort(angles)]\n\ndef centroid(v,r):\n z=points(v,r);ref=z.mean(0);area=0.;moment=np.zeros(3)\n for a,b in zip(z,np.roll(z,-1,axis=0)):\n  ar=np.linalg.norm(np.cross(a-ref,b-ref))/2\n  area+=ar;moment+=ar*(ref+a+b)/3\n return moment/area\n\ndef nearest(v,r):\n d=sum(v)-r;ell=np.maximum(v-d,0);u=np.minimum(v,d);s=r-sum(ell)\n lo=0.;hi=max(u)\n for _ in range(60):\n  t=(lo+hi)/2\n  if sum(np.minimum(u,t))<s:lo=t\n  else:hi=t\n return ell+np.minimum(u,(lo+hi)/2)\n\nn=0;bad=[]\nfor vv in product(range(1,7),repeat=3):\n v=np.array(vv,dtype=float)\n for r in range(1,sum(vv)):\n  expected=r<=min(v) or sum(v)-r<=min(v) or min(v)==max(v)\n  got=np.linalg.norm(centroid(v,r)-nearest(v,r))<1e-8\n  n+=1\n  if expected\"'!=got:bad.append((vv,r,expected,got))\nprint(n,'\"'integer instances checked; discrepancies:',bad)\nprint('Example centroid:',centroid(np.array([1.,2.,2.]),2),'nearest:',nearest(np.array([1.,2.,2.]),2))\nPY\nOPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 python /work/sol_check.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
